---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MathCard from '../components/MathCard.astro';
import Marquee from '../components/Marquee.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';

const plan = [
	'Read the competitive fair-price region from the quote book, on-chain, before the swap settles.',
	'Step in only when the trade is being filled on the wrong side of it — never when it moves toward fair.',
	'Fill part of the order from the hook’s buffer at a better price; recover the cost from solvers; send the surplus to LPs.',
];

const parameters = [
	['Arbitrageur commits', 'a stake + a quote', 'No inventory, no custody. Capital is committed only for the seconds it takes to sweep the hook’s inventory after winning.'],
	['MAX_FILL_BPS', '30% of the order', 'The largest share of a swap the hook will fill from its own buffer. The rest routes to the pool as a smaller trade.'],
	['HOOK_EDGE_BPS', '20% of the gap', 'Margin the hook keeps between the pool price and the runner-up belief. Lower ⇒ better for the swapper, thinner for LPs.'],
	['MIN_STAKE', '0.1 ETH', 'Bond posted before a quote counts as live — slashing collateral, never working capital.'],
	['MAX_QUOTE_DURATION', '5 minutes', 'Longest a belief stays valid. Stale prices expire themselves.'],
	['Hook permissions', 'beforeSwap · beforeSwapReturnDelta', 'The two flags mined into the hook address. The delta path only ever returns more output per input.'],
];

const without = [
	'Your trade pushes the pool past what the market thinks the pair is worth.',
	'The pool fills you at that worse price anyway.',
	'A searcher arbitrages the gap back afterward and keeps all of it.',
	'You read your fill and find out what it cost.',
];

const with_ = [
	'The hook sees the same push — and that your fill is now on the wrong side of fair.',
	'It fills part of your order itself, at a price between the pool and the runner-up belief.',
	'Your total output is higher than the plain pool would have given. Always.',
	'A solver later buys the hook’s position at second price; the surplus goes to LPs.',
];

const cards = [
	{
		title: 'We stopped trying to hide',
		body: 'Most answers to this ask you to trust something new — a private relay, an encrypted mempool, someone’s reputation. We assume your trade is visible to everyone, because it usually is, and work from there.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We only step in when it helps',
		body: 'The hook checks whether your swap is being filled on the wrong side of the competitive price. If the trade is moving toward fair, the hook does nothing at all — your good trade stays entirely yours.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We priced the intervention off the runner-up',
		body: 'The hook never uses the best belief to price your fill. It uses the second one, and keeps a fixed margin below it. Bidding your honest number stays the dominant strategy, and one aggressive quote can’t drag the fill.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We guaranteed vanilla-or-better',
		body: 'The partial fill is priced strictly better than the pool, and what’s left is a smaller, lower-impact swap. There is no input for which the hooked execution comes out worse than the plain pool.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We stopped asking arbitrageurs for capital',
		body: 'Solvers post a price. When a swap leaves the hook holding inventory, a solver later buys it at second price and hedges externally. Nothing sits in a vault waiting for a trade.',
	},
	{
		title: 'We made thin volatile pairs viable',
		body: 'Loss-versus-rebalancing is why volatile pools need fat fees, which kills their volume. Route the recaptured value to LPs and the fee no longer has to cover it — a low fee and live liquidity can coexist.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Hyberbola"
	description="A Uniswap v4 hook that fills part of an unfairly-priced swap itself, at a better price, and routes the recaptured value to LPs."
>
	<MathCard />

	<main>
		<header class="bar">
			<a class="mark" href="/">
				<Logo class="mark-glyph" size={24} />
				<span>Hyberbola</span>
			</a>
			<a class="bar-cta" href="/swap">Open Console →</a>
		</header>

		<section class="hero">
			<div class="headline-wrap">
				<Marquee />
				<h1>Your swap's bodyguard hook, 
					<em>funded by the people who used to mug it.</em></h1>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="prose">
			<p>
				Every trade that moves a constant-product pool carries extractable value, and today it
				goes to whoever is fastest. Blocking that has been tried from every direction — private
				relays, encrypted mempools, fee surcharges — and each one asks you to trust something
				new. None of them change the fact that the value exists.
			</p>
			<p>
				So do not fight it, and do not try to redistribute a loss after the fact. Catch it
				earlier. The card on the right derives the price the market actually believes a pair is
				worth, checks whether your swap is being filled on the wrong side of it, and — only then —
				fills part of your order from the hook's own buffer at a better price.
			</p>
			<p>
				The check is not an estimate. The fair region falls out of the pool's invariant and the
				staked quotes, it is read on-chain before the swap settles, and the fill is priced so that
				your total execution is never worse than the plain pool.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="plan">
			<ol>
				{
					plan.map((item, i) => (
						<li>
							<span class="num">{i + 1}</span>
							<span>{item}</span>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="prose">
			<p>
				Hyberbola is a Uniswap v4 hook. Arbitrageurs stake, then post the price they actually
				believe a pair is worth. The best and second-best live beliefs bracket a fair-price
				region. When a swap arrives, the hook simulates its vanilla execution and asks one
				question: does this trade push the pool to the far side of that region?
			</p>
			<p>
				If not — the swap is moving price toward fair, or there are no live beliefs — the hook
				returns nothing and the swap is an ordinary swap. If it does, the hook fills up to a
				third of the order itself, from a small hook-owned buffer, at a price set between the pool
				and the <em>runner-up</em> belief. The rest routes to the pool as a smaller, lower-impact
				trade.
			</p>
			<p>
				Because the fill is strictly better than the pool and the remainder has less impact, the
				swapper's total output beats the vanilla execution — every time the hook acts. Pricing off
				the second belief, not the first, means no single aggressive quote can move the fill, and
				honest bidding stays dominant.
			</p>
			<p>
				The fill leaves the hook holding inventory it bought slightly cheap. A solver later sweeps
				it at the runner-up belief and hedges externally, keeping only the gap to the best belief;
				the sweep refills the buffer and donates the surplus to the pool's LPs. No vault, no
				capital sitting idle waiting for a swap.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="params">
			<h2>Parameters, as deployed</h2>
			<dl>
				{
					parameters.map(([name, value, note]) => (
						<div class="param">
							<dt>{name}</dt>
							<dd class="param-value">{value}</dd>
							<dd class="param-note">{note}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section class="quote">
			<blockquote>The MEV was never the problem. Who kept it was.</blockquote>
		</section>

		<section class="versus">
			<h2>Same trade, two worlds</h2>
			<div class="versus-grid">
				<div class="versus-col">
					<span class="versus-label">On an ordinary pool</span>
					<ol>
						{without.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
					</ol>
				</div>
				<div class="versus-col versus-col-lit">
					<span class="versus-label">On this one</span>
					<ol>
						{with_.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
					</ol>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="cards">
			<h2>What we did</h2>
			<div class="card-grid">
				{
					cards.map((card) => (
						<article class="ecard">
							<h3>{card.title}</h3>
							<p>{card.body}</p>
						</article>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="status">
			<h2>Status</h2>
			<p>
				The contracts are written, tested, and deployed to Unichain Sepolia with a seeded USDC/DAI
				pool. The console reads that deployment by default, or any other you point it at. No audit
				to point at yet.
			</p>
			<p>
				The vanilla-or-better floor is structural — it holds no matter what anyone quotes. What is
				not done hardens the rest: a pool-TWAP floor on the sweep price, so a sybil quoter can’t
				suppress the LP donation; the external-venue settlement that lets a solver clear the hook’s
				inventory at scale; fuzz and invariant suites. The swap path — the decision, the partial
				fill, the floor — is the part that stands.
			</p>
			<a class="cta" href="/swap">Open the console →</a>
		</section>

		<footer>
			<span class="dim">Uniswap v4 hook · MIT</span>
			<a href="/swap">Console</a>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		width: var(--col-left);
		padding: 0 var(--step-6) 0 var(--step-5);
	}

	section {
		padding-bottom: var(--step-7);
	}

	.bar {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		padding: var(--step-4) 0 0;
	}

	.mark {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 10px;
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: 20px;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.mark-glyph {
		color: var(--ink);
		flex: none;
	}

	.bar-cta {
		flex: none;
		padding: 8px 15px;
		font-size: 13px;
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 999px;
		transition:
			color 160ms ease,
			border-color 160ms ease;
	}

	.bar-cta:hover {
		color: var(--ink);
		border-color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.hero {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: calc(100vh - var(--step-6));
		padding-bottom: var(--step-6);
	}

	.headline-wrap {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
	}

	h1 {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		max-width: 22ch;
		font-size: var(--hl-size);
		line-height: var(--hl-lead);
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}

	h1 em {
		font-style: normal;
		color: #d9a066;
	}

	.prose p + p {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
	}

	.prose p {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.plan ol li {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 62ch;
		padding: var(--step-2) 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.plan ol li:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.num {
		flex: none;
		width: 1.5rem;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	h2 {
		margin-bottom: var(--step-4);
		font-size: var(--type-body);
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	dl {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.param {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 15rem 1fr;
		gap: 2px var(--step-3);
		padding: var(--step-2) 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.param:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	dt {
		grid-row: span 2;
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: 13px;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	dd {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.param-note {
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.quote blockquote {
		max-width: 20ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 36px);
		line-height: 1.2;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.versus-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.versus-col {
		padding: var(--step-3);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	.versus-col-lit {
		border-color: rgba(217, 160, 102, 0.35);
		background: rgba(217, 160, 102, 0.045);
	}

	.versus-label {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: var(--step-3);
		font-size: 12px;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.versus-col-lit .versus-label {
		color: #d9a066;
	}

	.versus-col ol {
		counter-reset: step;
	}

	.versus-col li {
		position: relative;
		padding: 0 0 var(--step-3) var(--step-4);
		counter-increment: step;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.versus-col li:last-child {
		padding-bottom: 0;
	}

	.versus-col li::before {
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		content: counter(step);
		color: var(--ink-faint);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.versus-col-lit li {
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.card-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 68ch;
	}

	.ecard {
		padding: var(--step-3);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 12px;
		transition: border-color 200ms ease;
	}

	.ecard:hover {
		border-color: #3d3d3d;
	}

	.ecard h3 {
		margin-bottom: var(--step-2);
		font-size: 17px;
		font-weight: 300;
		letter-spacing: -0.015em;
	}

	.ecard p {
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.dim {
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	.status p {
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.status p + p {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
	}

	.cta {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: var(--step-4);
		padding-bottom: 3px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	.cta:hover {
		border-color: var(--ink-dim);
	}

	.fine {
		margin-top: var(--step-3);
		max-width: 46ch;
		color: var(--ink-faint);
	}

	footer {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--step-5);
		padding: var(--step-4) 0 var(--step-5);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	footer a:last-child {
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		main {
			width: auto;
			padding: 0 var(--gap) calc(var(--card-h) + var(--step-4));
		}

		.hero {
			min-height: calc(100vh - var(--card-h) - var(--step-5));
		}

		section {
			padding-bottom: var(--step-6);
		}

		.param {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}

		dt {
			grid-row: auto;
		}

		.versus-grid,
		.card-grid {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
